        <section id="view-setup" hidden>
          <div id="setup-summary" class="callout"></div>
          <div id="setup-controls" class="setup-grid">
            <article class="setup-card">
              <h2>1. Choose your sources</h2>
              <p>
                Use Settings → Import chats for a ChatGPT export. Local Codex history is
                optional. Saving a source choice does not scan it; select Sync
                workspace when ready.
              </p>
              <form id="source-form" class="form-grid">
                <label class="check"
                  ><input id="codex-enabled" type="checkbox" />Capture local
                  Codex history</label
                >
                <label
                  >Codex directory<input
                    id="codex-path"
                    placeholder="/absolute/path/to/.codex"
                    autocomplete="off"
                /></label>
                <button type="submit">Save source choice</button>
              </form>
            </article>
            <article class="setup-card">
              <h2>2. Choose assistant access</h2>
              <p>
                An assistant with local file access can use your workspace
                through ASSISTANT.md. Give that file to your chosen assistant;
                creating it does not connect an account or activate memory.
              </p>
              <button id="make-guide">Create or refresh assistant guide</button>
              <p id="guide-path" class="source-details"></p>
              <p>
                Let your Chief of Staff use ChatGrep through its reusable skill.
                New workspaces include a copy connected to their paths.
                Preparing the folder does not install it in your assistant.
              </p>
              <button id="make-skill">Prepare Chief of Staff skill</button>
              <p id="skill-path" class="source-details"></p>
              <details>
                <summary>Load the skill in your assistant</summary>
                <p>
                  Give the assistant the full SKILL.md path and ask it to read
                  and use it. In Codex, you can instead copy the whole chatos
                  folder to your project's .agents/skills/chatos or your own
                  ~/.agents/skills/chatos, preserving the references and agents
                  folders. Do not replace a folder you have customized. Verify
                  that chatos appears in the skill picker, then try: Use $chatos
                  to find our earlier discussion about my current project and
                  cite the messages. Skill instructions need local file and
                  terminal access; a hosted chat cannot read this folder
                  automatically.
                </p>
              </details>
            </article>
            <article class="setup-card">
              <h2>3. Review reusable context</h2>
              <p>
                Import a context JSON artifact prepared from visible
                conversations. Inspect its text, sources, scope and uncertainty
                before accepting it. Accepted notes become searchable; they are
                not installed as host instructions.
              </p>
              <details>
                <summary>Ask your AI to prepare an artifact</summary>
                <p>
                  Use only messages and files you can actually inspect. Separate
                  explicit preferences from suggestions. Return JSON with
                  schema_version: 1, kind: profile, preferences or
                  project_context, body, created_at (ISO timestamp with
                  timezone), generated_by, source_references (list), and
                  uncertainties (list). State missing evidence; do not claim
                  access to hidden memory. I will review before accepting.
                </p>
              </details>
              <label
                >Context artifact<input
                  id="artifact-file"
                  type="file"
                  accept=".json"
              /></label>
              <div id="artifact-list" class="artifact-list"></div>
              <div id="artifact-review"></div>
            </article>
            <article class="setup-card">
              <h2>4. Take context to another app</h2>
              <p>
                Create a verified local folder of Markdown and JSON. Nothing is
                uploaded. Review it before supplying files to another assistant.
                Missing messages and attachments are not recovered.
              </p>
              <form id="handoff-form" class="form-grid">
                <label
                  >Include<select id="handoff-selection">
                    <option value="chat">One conversation</option>
                    <option value="project">One project</option>
                    <option value="all">
                      All captured conversations, including archived
                    </option>
                  </select></label
                >
                <label id="handoff-chat-label"
                  >Conversation<select id="handoff-chat"></select
                ></label>
                <label id="handoff-project-label" hidden
                  >Project<select id="handoff-project"></select
                ></label>
                <label class="check"
                  ><input id="handoff-context" type="checkbox" />Include
                  profile, preferences and accepted context</label
                >
                <button type="submit">Create portable bundle</button>
              </form>
              <div id="handoff-result" role="status"></div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>
